WHAT THIS IS

This repository is SOURCE-AVAILABLE: others can inspect the source, while use stays
restricted. That is the same broad category many vendors use when they publish code
without adopting permissive MIT/Apache/GPL terms — for example MongoDB SSPL-era choice,
Elastic’s licensed modules, Redis’s RSAL historical line, MariaDB-style BSL forks,
Business Source-style delayed-OSS forks, PolyForm templated restrictive licenses —
each differ in detail — this template is bespoke to Licensor.

This agreement is NOT an Open Source Initiative (OSI)-approved license.


